Comment: 0,0:23:39.98,0:23:40.07,Default,chptr,0,0,0,,{Preview}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.53,0:00:10.37,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,Apologies. {Excuse me.}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.20,0:00:13.20,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.29,0:00:16.87,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,I'm the sorcerer who put up a barrier here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.46,0:00:21.96,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,This place was chosen \Nfor people to kill each other, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.75,0:00:26.05,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, it's nothing to be proud of.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.63,0:00:28.30,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,Kill each other?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.84,0:00:33.05,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,Could you please not do that at my place?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.02,0:00:37.85,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,You're funny.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.52,0:00:42.15,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,There's an old execution ground \Nnot far from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.15,0:00:44.69,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,The barrier is centered around that.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.69,0:00:47.15,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,100)}It covers a radius of five to six kilometers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.78,0:00:51.03,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,0)}Creating this barrier was already quite the task,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.03,0:00:54.16,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,100)}so I can't impose restrictions that are too unreasonable.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.66,0:00:59.91,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,0)}Those of you who were inside the barrier from the start \Nhave the right to leave it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.83,0:01:02.33,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,You get one chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.00,0:01:06.96,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,If you wish, you could wake up outside the barrier.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.97,0:01:10.09,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,Would you like to?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.63,0:01:12.84,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,Wake up?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.47,0:01:16.22,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,Is this a dream?
Comment: 0,0:01:16.22,0:01:20.52,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,The space between dreams and reality is a curse. {this line doesn't flow at all as the response to her question}
Comment: 0,0:01:16.22,0:01:20.52,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,100)}This is the space between \Ndreams and reality—call it magic. {this is him trying to explain what a curse is to people who don't know what curses are without making it sound ominous, so he uses a simpler and neutral term for it}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.22,0:01:20.52,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,100)}This is the space between \Ndreams and reality. It's a curse. {i don't think we should change this tbh, he's just saying "curse (neutral)" but at the end of the day it's still a curse}
Comment: 0,0:01:16.22,0:01:19.02,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,This is the space between dreams and reality.
Comment: 0,0:01:19.02,0:01:20.52,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,100)}It's a curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.57,0:01:26.90,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,Be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.90,0:01:28.28,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,Take it slowly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.78,0:01:32.03,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,100)}The hasty ones are already outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.43,0:02:00.89,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,Oh, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.89,0:02:02.77,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,I nearly forgot to mention it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.31,0:02:07.52,Default,Kenjaku,0,0,0,,Thank you for being friends with my son.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.23,0:02:07.52,Default,Iguchi,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HA0&}Sasaki! {this one's barely audible} {i'd say it's audible enough}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.40,0:02:09.53,Default,Iguchi,0,0,0,,{\alpha&H40&}Sasaki!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.11,0:02:11.28,Default,Iguchi,0,0,0,,{\alpha&H20&}Sasaki!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.69,0:02:12.49,Default,Iguchi,0,0,0,,Sasaki!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.53,0:02:16.70,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,Iguchi!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.70,0:02:19.95,Default,Iguchi,0,0,0,,I'm so glad to see someone I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.08,0:02:24.83,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,Where are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.33,0:02:28.67,Default,Iguchi,0,0,0,,Somewhere between Kotodai and Hirose Street.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.67,0:02:30.05,Default,Iguchi,0,0,0,,More importantly, look at that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.05,0:02:33.80,Default,Iguchi,0,0,0,,As a member of the occult club, what's your opinion on that?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.55,0:02:36.97,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,{\an8}On that?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.77,0:02:43.56,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,Can I talk about the dream I had?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.31,0:02:47.73,Default,Iguchi,0,0,0,,Everyone's had it. \NWas it the long-haired guy in monk's robes?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.40,0:02:51.78,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,D-Did he say something about his son to you, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.78,0:02:54.45,Default,Iguchi,0,0,0,,Huh? No, first I've heard of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.87,0:02:59.95,Default,Sasaki,0,0,0,,Itadori?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.75,0:04:34.88,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,For real?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.30,0:04:37.42,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Gojo{**-san} got sealed?
Dialogue: 1,0:04:37.67,0:04:39.01,Default,Three,0,0,0,,For real.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.67,0:04:39.01,Default,Three,0,0,0,,{\pos(550,1015)}For real.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.67,0:04:39.01,Default,Three,0,0,0,,{\pos(1370,1015)}For real.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.55,0:04:43.39,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Damn!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.39,0:04:47.27,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,Also, sorry to mention this as an aside, \Nbut the principal's dead, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.90,0:04:53.56,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Panda{**-senpai}?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.56,0:04:56.94,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,Sorry for not telling you earlier, but it's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.57,0:04:59.49,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,It's all right, Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.49,0:05:01.16,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,He didn't die in Shibuya.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.16,0:05:03.49,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,He got into a scuffle \Nwith the higher-ups after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.03,0:05:06.54,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,That doesn't make it any better.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.54,0:05:08.96,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,The principal was your...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.96,0:05:12.00,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,I know, and I said it's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.00,0:05:13.08,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,Thanks, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.75,0:05:17.80,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,If you say so, \Nthen there's nothing more for us to add.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.80,0:05:18.76,Default,Kirara,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.55,0:05:23.47,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Still, that's everyone \Nwho's had my back all at once...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.47,0:05:28.43,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,I haven't been this bummed out \Nsince I watched Yakul get shot in the ass with an arrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.43,0:05:30.85,Default,Three,0,0,0,,{\i1}What a nice life he's lived.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.43,0:05:30.85,Default,Three,0,0,0,,{\i1\pos(430,136)}What a nice life he's lived.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.43,0:05:30.85,Default,Three,0,0,0,,{\i1\pos(1510,136)}What a nice life he's lived.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.85,0:05:35.11,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Alright. I'll help settle this Culling Game.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.57,0:05:39.49,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Don't get it twisted, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.03,0:05:42.32,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,This ain't me getting soft. {I'm not doing this out of sympathy.}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.32,0:05:45.70,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,We're cutting a deal here. Got it?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.70,0:05:50.37,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Once we clean up this Culling Game mess, \Nyou're gonna help me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.37,0:05:55.04,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,You're trying to get in on the revisions \Nto the Jujutsu Regulations, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.04,0:06:01.84,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,Now that the existence of curses has gone public, \Nthere's sure to be some kind of revision,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.84,0:06:04.18,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,but what exactly are you hoping for?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.34,0:06:08.81,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Whatever it is, I doubt it'll be that hard to secure.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.81,0:06:09.85,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.85,0:06:13.69,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,What the hell would {\i1}you{\i0} know about it, \NSea Urchin Head, huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.35,0:06:17.06,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,I'm the head of the Zenin Clan.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.15,0:06:21.69,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.90,0:06:26.74,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wait, wait, wait, wait, what the fuck?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.74,0:06:30.20,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm sorry for the other two, \Nbut that's the most shocking thing I've heard today!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.20,0:06:35.21,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,{\i1}With one of the Three Great Clans backing me up, \NI could easily influence the revisions! {the revisions to the regulations?}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.21,0:06:40.92,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll have to keep the Zenin Clan from interfering with \Nthe Fight Club, but that's a problem for later.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.92,0:06:43.34,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Sea Urchin Head!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.34,0:06:44.55,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,It's Fushiguro.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.55,0:06:45.68,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,{*}Fushiguro, my man{*Fushiguro-kun}!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.14,0:06:52.02,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Let's be friends?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.02,0:06:52.89,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.56,0:06:59.65,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,All right, now we just need to decide \Nwho's heading to which colony.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.65,0:07:01.23,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,Yuta went to Miyagi, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.23,0:07:02.23,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}Ding-dong, {\alpha&HFF&}ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.23,0:07:02.53,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}Ding-dong, ding-dong, {\alpha&HFF&}ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.53,0:07:02.86,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}Ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, {\alpha&HFF&}ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.86,0:07:03.15,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}Ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, {\alpha&HFF&}ding-dong, ding-dong!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.15,0:07:03.40,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}Ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, {\alpha&HFF&}ding-dong!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.40,0:07:05.03,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}Ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.03,0:07:10.24,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,A player has added a new rule to the Culling Game!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.24,0:07:14.00,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Rule 9: Players shall be able to view \Nthe following information on other players:
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.00,0:07:20.34,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,name, points, number of rules added, and current colony.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.17,0:07:22.67,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,I am Kogane!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.67,0:07:25.84,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,The interface between players \Nand the Culling Game!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.18,0:07:28.59,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Did that thing just switch personalities?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.59,0:07:31.76,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,The first part was an announcement \Nfrom the Culling Game!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.76,0:07:37.65,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,I am now speaking as the interface \Nassigned to the player Itadori Yuji!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.02,0:07:42.07,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama} did mention \Nsomething about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.07,0:07:43.86,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,No, this isn't right!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.86,0:07:47.20,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Why would Itadori be counted \Nas a player already?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.20,0:07:50.78,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Aside from those Kenjaku gave \Ncursed techniques or cursed objects,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.78,0:07:54.50,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,the only players should be \Nthose who have entered a colony!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.50,0:07:59.17,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(0,120)\bord4\c&H000000&}The ones like Itadori Yuji,\N whom I had absorb cursed objects.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.87,0:08:01.67,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(120,120)\an8\bord4\c&H000000&}...I painstakingly forged Binding Vows \Nover a thousand years.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.21,0:08:03.21,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(120,0)\bord4\c&H000000&}And it wasn't just sorcerers \Nthat I formed Binding Vows with.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:55.50,0:07:59.17,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(0,120)\blur0.8\bord0\c&H8EFF00&\alpha&H80&\pos(958,916)}The ones like Itadori Yuji,\N whom I had absorb cursed objects.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:57.87,0:08:01.67,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(120,120)\an8\blur0.8\bord0\c&H8EFF00&\alpha&H80&\pos(958,164)}...I painstakingly forged Binding Vows \Nover a thousand years.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:00.21,0:08:03.21,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(120,0)\blur0.8\bord0\c&H8EFF00&\alpha&H80&\pos(958,916)}And it wasn't just sorcerers \Nthat I formed Binding Vows with.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:55.50,0:07:59.17,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(0,120)\blur0.8\bord0\c&HF85FFF&\pos(962,916)}The ones like Itadori Yuji,\N whom I had absorb cursed objects.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:57.87,0:08:01.67,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(120,120)\an8\blur0.8\bord0\c&HF85FFF&\alpha&H80&\pos(962,164)}...I painstakingly forged Binding Vows \Nover a thousand years.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:00.21,0:08:03.21,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(120,0)\blur0.8\bord0\c&HF85FFF&\alpha&H80&\pos(962,916)}And it wasn't just sorcerers \Nthat I formed Binding Vows with.
Dialogue: 3,0:07:55.50,0:07:59.17,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(0,120)\blur0.8\bord0\c&HF9FFEE&}The ones like Itadori Yuji,\N whom I had absorb cursed objects.
Dialogue: 3,0:07:57.87,0:08:01.67,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(120,120)\an8\blur0.8\bord0\c&HF9FFEE&}...I painstakingly forged Binding Vows \Nover a thousand years.
Dialogue: 3,0:08:00.21,0:08:03.21,Default,Geto,0,0,164,,{\fad(120,0)\blur0.8\bord0\c&HF9FFEE&}And it wasn't just sorcerers \Nthat I formed Binding Vows with.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.21,0:08:08.13,Default,Gojo,0,0,0,,{\alpha&H20&}In reality, he was actually a human \Nwho existed over a thousand years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.13,0:08:09.51,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Sukuna.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.51,0:08:10.39,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,{\fs32\bord2.2\shad1.2\pos(1694,218)}Sukuna?
Comment: 0,0:08:09.51,0:08:10.39,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,{\an8}Sukuna?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.72,0:08:12.81,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I think Sukuna was one of the sorcerers
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.81,0:08:15.98,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,who entered a contract with Kenjaku and became a cursed object.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.35,0:08:20.10,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}So participating in the Culling Game \Nwas part of the contract?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.10,0:08:21.86,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,It still doesn't make sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.27,0:08:24.86,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,You swallowed Sukuna's finger \Nof your own free will.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.86,0:08:26.03,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,I witnessed it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.99,0:08:31.32,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Let's discuss this later. {nooo you're close to figuring something out}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.82,0:08:36.12,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Itadori, could you have Kogane pull up \Nthe players' information right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.46,0:08:39.50,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Kogane, can you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.50,0:08:40.54,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Sure can!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.17,0:08:44.13,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Ta-da!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.92,0:08:47.26,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,This guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.80,0:08:50.13,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,So he originally had 200 points?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.01,0:08:53.43,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,I wonder why he added this rule.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.43,0:08:57.56,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,He's killed 40 people at the very least, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.56,0:09:00.06,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I doubt he has nice intentions.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.06,0:09:05.78,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Still, this means we might be able to progress \Nthrough the Culling Game without killing anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.23,0:09:10.61,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Kogane, can you show a list of players \Nwith 100 points or more?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.61,0:09:14.74,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Well, I'm assigned to Itadori Yuji, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.74,0:09:16.37,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Oh, it's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.37,0:09:18.25,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Go ahead and do what he asked.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.25,0:09:25.80,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Aside from people like Tsumiki who got caught up in this and are in a rush to escape, {basically he says there are two types of players: ones who got dragged into this and just wanna gtfo, and ones who joined in willingly by forging a binding vow with kenny in the past}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.80,0:09:31.18,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,the incarnated sorcerers from the past must have had \Ntheir own motives for contracting with Kenjaku.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.18,0:09:34.18,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,They don't have any real reason to add rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.55,0:09:38.60,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,If there's anyone else like Kashimo \Nsitting on an excess of points...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.60,0:09:39.98,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Oh, I get it!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.98,0:09:45.27,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,We find someone with 100 points or more \Nwho has no interest in adding rules...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.27,0:09:48.98,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,...and make them add a rule \Nto let Tsumiki escape the Culling Game!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.24,0:09:49.99,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Here you are.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:52.15,0:09:53.36,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,There's another one!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.74,0:09:54.70,Default,Both,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.28,0:09:57.91,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,The first thing we need to do \Nis deal with Rule 8.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.91,0:09:58.37,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.74,0:10:01.21,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,What was Rule 8 again?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.58,0:10:04.71,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\blur1\q2\c&H000000&}It's the one that says if your points don't change within 19 days, \Nyour technique gets stripped, leading to death.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:01.58,0:10:08.50,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\q2}It's the one that says if your points don't change within 19 days, \Nyour technique gets stripped, leading to death.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.50,0:10:14.26,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,To counter that, we add a rule saying, \N"Players can transfer points to each other."
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.72,0:10:17.56,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Then we can keep passing points \Namong ourselves
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.56,0:10:20.85,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,and avoid dying from \Nhaving our techniques stripped.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.27,0:10:22.85,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,If possible, we add one more.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.85,0:10:28.27,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,A rule that says, \N"Players may expend points to leave the Culling Game."
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.27,0:10:32.70,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Wouldn't that conflict with the rule \Nprohibiting any long-lasting effect? {when did hakari learn about the rules? did he watch that summary video they made?}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.70,0:10:34.41,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think it would.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.41,0:10:40.83,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,But if we add a condition like dragging a non-player \Ninto the Culling Game as a substitute, it might work.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.83,0:10:42.58,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,True.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.58,0:10:44.96,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Would Kogane be making the call on that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.96,0:10:48.13,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Either way, we know what we need to do now.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.13,0:10:48.92,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.63,0:10:53.01,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,While searching for the Angel \Nto break the seal on the Prison Realm,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.01,0:10:58.01,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,we'll go after Kashimo Hajime and Higuruma Hiromi
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.01,0:11:00.64,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,and hunt them down.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.18,0:11:05.98,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Yeah, there's no "Angel" on here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.40,0:11:10.23,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,That probably isn't her real name, \Njust like you and Sukuna. {oda level foreshadowing} {CR: Just like you're not listed as Sukuna.}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.73,0:11:14.61,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama} said she was in eastern Tokyo.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.61,0:11:17.11,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,That would be Colony No. 2, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.62,0:11:19.49,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,You guys know what she looks like?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.12,0:11:21.91,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Apparently, we'll know when we see her. {ofc you will}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.91,0:11:24.25,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Are you sure about that? {CR: Is that gonna work out?}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.87,0:11:26.17,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Well, whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.17,0:11:28.17,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Panda and I will take Tokyo No. 2.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.17,0:11:30.84,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Fushiguro{**-kyun} and Itadori can take No. 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.84,0:11:32.50,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Kirara, stand by outside the barriers.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.50,0:11:33.59,Default,Kirara,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.59,0:11:34.72,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Sound good?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.13,0:11:36.18,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,What's your reasoning?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.18,0:11:40.76,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Going by points, this Kashimo's the strongest one, \Nso it makes sense for me to take him.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.76,0:11:42.93,Default,Kirara,0,0,0,,I'm being left out? {fuck you gon do} {CR: I'm being excluded?}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.93,0:11:46.64,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,You've got a keen nose, Panda, \Nso focus on finding the Angel.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.27,0:11:52.48,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,The fact that we haven't heard from Okkotsu \Nmeans we can't use cell phones inside the barriers.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.48,0:11:55.90,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,So we'll need someone \Nto keep tabs on what's going on outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.90,0:11:57.28,Default,Kirara,0,0,0,,Fiiine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.28,0:11:58.41,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.78,0:12:01.33,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,It might be best for me and Fushiguro to be split up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.33,0:12:02.08,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Sukuna is—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.08,0:12:02.95,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Shut up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.37,0:12:04.66,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,The hell?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.66,0:12:07.96,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,The other three can't change their roles.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.96,0:12:09.33,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,So quit being selfish.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.33,0:12:10.92,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm{\i0} being selfish?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.92,0:12:12.92,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I'm just worrying about you here!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.92,0:12:15.71,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Are you going to say that every time?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.71,0:12:18.43,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,It's annoying and it's a waste of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.43,0:12:19.51,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\pos(1111,1015)}Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.93,0:12:19.51,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\pos(800,1015)}Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.51,0:12:20.80,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,No fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.30,0:12:24.64,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Yo, I'm Kogane!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.64,0:12:30.48,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Inside this barrier is the Culling Game, where players fight to the death!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.48,0:12:34.19,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Once you step inside, \Nyou, too, become a player!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.19,0:12:37.70,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Are you still willing to enter?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.70,0:12:38.32,Default,Hakari,0,0,0,,Damn right!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.32,0:12:38.95,Default,Panda,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.95,0:12:40.28,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,No issues here.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.83,0:12:46.00,Default,Hanyu,0,0,0,,Hey, Amai!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.08,0:12:50.58,Default,Hanyu,0,0,0,,I've been waiting forever for your signal.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.96,0:12:54.75,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Uh, well, I hear you,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.75,0:12:57.34,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,but there's nothing I can do \Nif no one's showing up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.34,0:12:58.05,Default,Hanyu,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.17,0:13:02.30,Default,Hanyu,0,0,0,,Are you talking back to me now?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.26,0:13:06.02,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,N-No! Look, I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.02,0:13:07.73,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Please forgive me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.35,0:13:09.89,Default,Hanyu,0,0,0,,If you start mouthing off again,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.06,0:13:13.77,Default,Hanyu,0,0,0,,I'll run you over.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.94,0:13:17.53,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,The incarnated sorcerers \Nare the ones to watch out for.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.53,0:13:19.32,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Yeah, totally.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.82,0:13:22.61,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Can you explain why though, Fushiguro{**-kun}? {i sure hope the joke comes across}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.62,0:13:26.08,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Some of them are from a thousand years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.08,0:13:29.83,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,People valued life very differently \Njust a hundred or two hundred years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.83,0:13:31.50,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Plus, they're sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.50,0:13:35.46,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,A fight to the death is par for the course for them. \NIn fact, they {\i1}want{\i0} to die fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.46,0:13:38.84,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,That might even be why \Nthey forged contracts with Kenjaku.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.84,0:13:42.89,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,There's a strong chance that \NKashimo and Higuruma are past sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.89,0:13:44.89,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Don't expect a proper negotiation.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.89,0:13:47.89,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Then the other aggressive ones \Nare gonna be curses, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.27,0:13:49.73,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Especially at night.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.31,0:13:54.02,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,That said, a modern day sorcerer \Nwho got dragged into this like Tsumiki
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.02,0:13:57.15,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,might be open to exchanging information.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.11,0:14:00.99,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}Yo, I'm Kogane!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.40,0:14:06.95,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}Inside this barrier is the Culling Game, where players fight to the death!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.95,0:14:10.29,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}Once you step inside, \Nyou, too, become a player!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.29,0:14:13.00,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}Are you still willing to enter?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.00,0:14:15.42,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Yeah. No issues here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.75,0:14:20.42,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Fushiguro Megumi has joined the Culling Game.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.42,0:14:22.42,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Would you like to see the rules?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.42,0:14:24.51,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,No. I'm good.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.51,0:14:24.97,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Aw.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.26,0:14:26.05,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.05,0:14:26.80,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.80,0:14:29.47,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,First, we gather information on Higuruma.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.81,0:14:30.72,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.72,0:14:31.60,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.15,0:14:38.36,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Where's Fushiguro?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.82,0:14:43.20,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}When a player enters one of the Culling Game barriers,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.20,0:14:48.08,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}they are randomly teleported \Nto one of nine designated locations.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.08,0:14:52.83,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}It was a rule of the barriers, \Nseparate from the rules of the Culling Game.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.83,0:14:55.46,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}At those nine locations, they lay in wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.75,0:14:56.67,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Here's one!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.00,0:15:01.59,Default,Narration,0,0,0,,{\an8}Players who targeted those disoriented \Nby this unmentioned phenomenon.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.93,0:15:12.56,Default,Narration,0,0,0,,{\an8}Newbie-hunters.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.23,0:15:16.56,Default,Hanyu,0,0,0,,{\i1}This one's tough!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.56,0:15:20.61,Default,Hanyu,0,0,0,,{\i1}Most would've turned into mincemeat \Nby that, but he's still kicking.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.61,0:15:21.98,Default,Hanyu,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's not your average Joe. {He is specialz.}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.45,0:15:34.45,Default,Hanyu,0,0,0,,Darling, let's meet up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.79,0:15:39.79,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}She went down easily. {is there any indication that this is internal thought? a couple lines later he is speaking out loud} {i'll still keep the italics since this was internal in the manga and also the voice acting is a little different}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.79,0:15:41.96,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I need to ask her about Higuruma.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.96,0:15:44.21,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then I have to find Fushiguro.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.80,0:15:45.88,Default,Haba,0,0,0,,What the hell?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.76,0:15:49.09,Default,Haba,0,0,0,,What did you do to my woman?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.72,0:15:51.51,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Guess I can just ask him.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.85,0:15:53.93,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Haba{**-san} flew in.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.93,0:15:55.98,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Was Hanyu{**-san} taken out?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.98,0:15:58.69,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where have I seen that guy before...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.94,0:16:01.15,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Itadori?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.15,0:16:04.86,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,It hurts! It hurts so bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.86,0:16:07.86,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why{\i0} are you doing this to me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.86,0:16:09.87,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,You're the one who attacked me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.24,0:16:11.16,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.16,0:16:13.49,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I didn't expect us \Nto get separated like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.83,0:16:14.75,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Well?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.04,0:16:18.08,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nue can't find him, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.08,0:16:21.04,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}This colony is much larger than Shibuya.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.04,0:16:23.34,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}We're probably over two kilometers apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.96,0:16:25.88,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}But we're headed to the same destination.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.88,0:16:29.30,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Do you know a sorcerer named Higuruma?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.80,0:16:33.64,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Men think they can just beat women \Ninto doing whatever they want, don't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.64,0:16:34.68,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Answer me!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.68,0:16:36.93,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Yes. I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.93,0:16:40.90,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Higuruma's that guy, right? The one with 100 points?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.56,0:16:43.15,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Do you know where he is?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.90,0:16:48.61,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Oh, I see how it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.58,0:17:05.09,Default,Haba,0,0,0,,{\i1}Dammit! He's one strong son of a bitch!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.01,0:17:14.89,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought I'd be in trouble \Nif he constantly had the high ground,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.89,0:17:17.93,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}but that propeller is his only means of attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.95,0:17:40.37,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}He has to get in close to kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.37,0:17:42.12,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll drag him indoors!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.31,0:17:58.47,Default,Haba,0,0,0,,I'll blend you into a smoothie!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.64,0:18:03.48,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's finally turned his head toward me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.73,0:18:10.28,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}That airplane woman was sturdy enough \Nto smash through buildings with me,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.28,0:18:12.74,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}yet a simple projectile took her out.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.74,0:18:18.33,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I bet their hair is the core of their technique. \NThey're weaker away from it. {you know, it would've made more sense if they strengthend their hair (which gives them their abilities) but in exchange the rest of their bodies were weaker, but the jp text explicitlty states there's a distance-based mechanic, which is kinda weird, but hey im not the author}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.33,0:18:19.66,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it a Binding Vow?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.66,0:18:23.04,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}No matter how tough it may be, \Nit's still their head.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.04,0:18:26.42,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I can land a hit, I can crack it open!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.14,0:18:39.89,Default,Haba,0,0,0,,Broke your fist, did ya?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.89,0:18:42.43,Default,Haba,0,0,0,,You just lost this battle! {denji would be so proud}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.74,0:18:53.82,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Nah, I didn't break anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.82,0:18:54.61,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Ow.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.61,0:18:57.03,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,I don't mind telling you,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.03,0:18:59.62,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,but I want you to do me a favor in return.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.45,0:19:02.70,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Say it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.70,0:19:05.33,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Say it, plea...?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.33,0:19:07.13,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Tell me, plea...?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.13,0:19:07.83,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Spit it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.00,0:19:10.00,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.76,0:19:13.55,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Will you be my knight?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.55,0:19:15.05,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Yeah, whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.39,0:19:19.76,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Am I that much of a bore? {Am I really no fun to tease?}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.76,0:19:21.39,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,I don't have time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.39,0:19:22.64,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Hurry it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.64,0:19:23.81,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Walk in front.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.81,0:19:25.64,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Do you even get it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.02,0:19:29.90,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,As my knight, you're supposed to \Nprotect me with your life!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.82,0:19:33.40,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,I will if you're telling me the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.32,0:19:37.78,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Hey, wake up.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.78,0:19:40.99,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I wanna ask about a sorcerer named Higuruma.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.41,0:19:44.29,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,I-Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.00,0:19:47.58,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,I know him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.21,0:19:50.29,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,That Higuruma guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.17,0:19:54.67,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,You know what will happen if you're lying, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.59,0:19:57.43,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm not like Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.43,0:20:00.01,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll earn those 100 points myself if I have to.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.43,0:20:02.81,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Can you stop referring to me that way?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.81,0:20:04.31,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Call me Remi.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.89,0:20:07.39,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,It's been a while. Remember me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.48,0:20:09.15,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.69,0:20:12.02,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}How does he know my name?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.36,0:20:16.03,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Oh, sorry. I guess you wouldn't know me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.03,0:20:18.32,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,You were famous, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.32,0:20:19.78,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,"Tiger of West Middle."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.16,0:20:22.66,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Oh! You're from my hometown!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.95,0:20:27.54,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Wait, so you're not \None of the past sorcerers?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.54,0:20:28.92,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Excuse me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.92,0:20:31.54,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Do I look that far behind the times?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.92,0:20:34.42,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Then what's your reason to fight?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.96,0:20:36.17,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Listen, you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.63,0:20:41.05,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,The non-player civilians got to leave the colony,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.60,0:20:44.81,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,but us players who were in the colony from the start
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.81,0:20:48.89,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,have been stuck in the Culling Game \Nfor {\i1}twelve days{\i0} now!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.35,0:20:52.36,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,I'm not doing this because I {\i1}want{\i0} to! {so she was a player from the start? why is she acting like she got caught up in this? there was an option for her to leave the colony at the start right? is she just lying?} {excellent fucking shot.}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.36,0:20:54.32,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,It's kill or be killed!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.90,0:20:59.24,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,You'll be dead before you find your reason to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.24,0:21:01.91,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Anyone can figure that out after twelve days here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.53,0:21:05.54,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,I've seen people go mad with power along the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.20,0:21:09.66,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Stop worrying about whether they're \Npast or modern sorcerers. {i.e. they're both dangerous} {it doesn't matter}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.00,0:21:14.92,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}So the past sorcerers have pushed \Nthe modern sorcerers into combat mode too?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.46,0:21:18.13,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I might have given Itadori bad advice, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.13,0:21:19.51,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.51,0:21:22.05,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Weren't you with those two?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.59,0:21:24.76,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,I was just their gofer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.76,0:21:26.89,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,They would've killed me at some point.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.89,0:21:27.47,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.93,0:21:31.60,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,It's about time you tell me where we're going.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.94,0:21:33.44,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Look!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.44,0:21:37.53,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,There's no guarantee \Nthat you won't kill me after I tell you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.86,0:21:39.95,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I see. Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.95,0:21:41.36,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,It's Amai.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.36,0:21:42.28,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Amai Rin.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.28,0:21:45.12,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What if you die before we get there?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.12,0:21:46.45,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,That's why! {\alpha&HFF&}You! Need to protect me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.45,0:21:47.41,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,That's why! You! {\alpha&HFF&}Need to protect me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.41,0:21:49.20,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,That's why! You! Need to protect me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.20,0:21:50.87,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,And use my name already!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.87,0:21:52.33,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Anything could happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.33,0:21:55.04,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Amai, where is Higuruma?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.04,0:21:58.59,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,All right, fine. I'll give you a rough location.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.59,0:22:01.55,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Strong ones gather where the city once thrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.55,0:22:03.22,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Plenty of resources there.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.22,0:22:04.30,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\pos(1440,1015)}Higuruma is in...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.80,0:22:04.89,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\pos(480,1015)}Higuruma is in...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.89,0:22:06.60,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\pos(480,1015)}Ikebukuro.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.43,0:22:06.85,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\pos(1440,1015)}Shinjuku.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.60,0:22:07.22,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\pos(480,1015)}Got it?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.85,0:22:07.97,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\pos(1440,1015)}Got it?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.86,0:23:44.44,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\an8}I just sense potential in the Culling Game.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.44,0:23:45.74,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\an8}Every person in this country will die.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.74,0:23:48.07,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\an8}You've been played.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.07,0:23:49.45,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\an8}I'm sorry, Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.45,0:23:51.20,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\an8}A sorcerer connected to Kenjaku!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.20,0:23:52.16,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\an8}I wanna talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.16,0:23:54.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\an8}We're having a retrial.
